  "description": "T1 London plane : Reduce lateral growth in lower to mid crown (to 10m height) to\rwest by 2 to 2.5m branch lengths to reduce overextended form over highway. \rReduce the lateral growth on the south, at 7 to 10m height by 1.5m branch lengths\rto give balanced form. Reduce by approx. 2 m laterally over the highway. Reduce\rfrom the façade as required to provide 5m clearance.\rT2 London plane: Remove crossing branch to southwest at 8m height. Reduce\rupper northeast limb at 18m height by 2.5 to 3m branch lengths to balance with\rremainder of crown. Reduce by approx. 2 m laterally over the highway. Reduce from\rthe facade as required to provide 5m clearance.\rT3 London plane : reduce low lateral to East at 7 to 10m height by pruning 2 to 2.5m\rlengths to balance with remainder of crown. Reduce by approx. 2 m laterally over the\rhighway. Reduce from the facade as required to provide 5m clearance.\rT4 London plane - Reduce mid to upper crown at 14 to 20m height to east, by 2 to\r2.5m branch lengths to balance with remainder of crown and reduce over extended\rlaterals in this direction. Reduce by approx. 2m laterally over the highway. Reduce\rfrom the facade as required to provide 5m clearance.\rT5 London plane: Reduce by approx. 2m laterally over the highway. Reduce from\rthe facade as required to provide 5m clearance.\rT6 London plane: Reduce by approx. 2m laterally over the highway. Reduce from\rthe facade as required to provide 5m clearance.\rT7 London plane - Prune to give 1m clearance from lamppost."
